<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maximilian of Egmond</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1509–1548</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Maximilian of Egmond, Count of Buren</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maximilian of Egmond (1509–1548), Count of Buren, was a general and stadtholder of Friesland in the service of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>. He led an army from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> to join the emperor in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-war">Schmalkaldic War</a> of 1546–1547 and received the county of Lingen, confiscated from Count Konrad of Tecklenburg. His only daughter Anna married William of Orange in 1551, bringing Buren and Lingen to the House of Orange.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maximilian-of-egmond.jpg" alt="Maximilian of Egmond" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tom Lemmens (talk) · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wapen_van_Egmont.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
